From da995d442507a370e6f9fa2e24d81bf5d02cdc36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:54:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: login for the web interface

The web interface (port 80) had no login: anyone on the network could
change every setting. Now every request goes through
WebAuth::beginRequest (civetweb begin_request): a page without a session
is sent to /login.html, an API call gets 401. Open without a login: the
login page and what it loads, /api/v1/auth/*, and requests from the
CosmosEx itself (127.0.0.1).

- On by default (WEBUI_LOGIN), password "thisisinsecure" until one is
  set; stored as PBKDF2-SHA256 with a random salt (WEBUI_PWHASH, libcrypto),
  compared in constant time.
- insecure.txt on the boot partition (WEBUI_INSECURE_FILE) switches the
  login off: the way back in when the password is forgotten.
- POST /api/v1/auth/login {"password"} sets a session cookie (128 random
  bits, HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, 30 days without use); POST
  /api/v1/auth/logout; GET /api/v1/auth/status. A wrong password waits
  1 s; 10 in a minute lock the login for a minute.
- Settings section "weblogin": enabled, insecureFile, defaultPassword;
  PUT {"enabled", "password"} (a new password ends the other logins).
- Links with -lcrypto.
